  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "For a quadratic integer a = p + q\\sqrt d \\in \\mathbb{Z}[\\sqrt d] with norm N(a) = p^2 - d q^2, let M = ((p, d q),(q, p)) be its companion matrix (\\det M = N(a)). The sequence x_n = \\Re(a^n) obeying x_{n+1} = 2p\\,x_n - N(a)\\,x_{n-1} satisfies the Cassini/Catalan identity x_{n-1} x_{n+1} - x_n^2 = (x_0 x_2 - x_1^2)\\,N(a)^{n-1}, derived from \\det(M^n) = (\\det M)^n = N(a)^n.",
    "plain": "AVAILABLE — Prove the Cassini/Catalan-type identity xₙ₋₁xₙ₊₁ − xₙ² = (constant)·(N(a))ⁿ from det(Mⁿ) = (det M)ⁿ = N(a)ⁿ, deriving the determinant identity directly from the companion-matrix closed form.",
